        "original_id": "771e3618-afb5-5eed-9741-f7da4c1da5db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Yale football, Notre Dame football\n- People: George Gipp, Walter Camp\n- Events: 1920 Yale football season\n- Topics: national champions, All-American honors\n\nFacts:\n- The 1920 Yale football season had no clear-cut champion.\n- The Official Yale Division I Football Records Book lists California, Georgia, Harvard, Notre Dame, and Princeton as national champions for that season.\n- Notre Dame was led by George Gipp during that season.\n- George Gipp was Notre Dame's first Walter Camp All-American.\n- George Gipp was nicknamed \"The Gipper.\"\n- George Gipp died before the end of 1920.",
